From 87483e7e19c58f1fa98070e7d5748742bd505e0a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vaxorcist <vaxorcist@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 11:59:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] SCP, HK: Common SDL2 sound support (sim_sound) and the RK07
 sound pilot

Sound for all simulators (sim_sound.c/.h), phases A and B:

- sim_sound is compiled into every simulator.  With SDL2 (USE_SIM_SOUND)
  it plays WAV samples through its own SDL audio device; without SDL2
  every playback call is a no-op while SET/SHOW SOUND, the realism flag
  and the power state still work.
- Mixer in the SDL audio callback: 64 voices, float summing with -6 dB
  headroom, soft limiter, master and group volumes (SYSTEM, DISK, TAPE,
  EVENT) with mutes, click-free fades, one-shot to loop chaining and
  random-phase loops.  Playback requests only queue a command.
- System sounds: RUN and BOOT power on (starting sound, running loop);
  stops at the prompt keep the power on; EXIT plays the stopping sound
  and waits, SET SOUND POWER=OFF switches off by hand.
- SET SOUND ENABLED switches on the realism mode (refused while a disk or
  tape is attached; disabled by default), including a per-simulator
  realistic THROTTLE unless the user set one (sim_timer: sim_throt_is_set).
- Unit loops for spindles, optional samples, file search in SET SOUND
  PATH, SIMH_SOUND_PATH, sound/<sim>/ beside or above the executable and
  ./sound/<sim>/.
- RK611 (HK): SET HKn ONLINE/OFFLINE (RUN/STOP buttons), SHOW HKn
  SPINDLE; in the realism mode ATTACH waits for ONLINE, spin-up time
  (SPINUP), UNLOAD spins down instead of detaching, realistic RK06/RK07
  seek, latency and transfer times, short/medium/long seek sounds
  (SEEK6S/SEEK6M/SEEK7S/SEEK7M), optional spindle sounds.
- Default sounds (per file, an own file wins): sound/default_cpu/ with
  recordings of a real VAX-11/750 (power relay and blower start, running
  blower as a seamless loop, power off and run-down), used by simulators
  that opt in (the vax750, also THROTTLE 300K, provisional);
  sound/default_disk/: synthetic seek sounds for every disk drive.  All
  sounds under the SIMH license.
- Builds: makefile (SDL2 audio for all simulators, NOSOUND=1), CMake
  (WITH_SOUND, simh_sound), descrip.mms.  The Visual Studio
  projects are not updated yet (they do not build sim_sound.c).

VMS boot fixes: the RK611 converts realistic durations to instructions
itself (at the throttle target rate), the realism mode starts the
throttle at power-on (THROT_DELAY 0), and the throttle measures freshly
with THROT_DELAY 0 (sim_timer: sim_throt_target_ips, sim_throt_set_delay).

Spin-up: SPINUP ms of simulated time while the CPU runs, wall time while
stopped at the sim> prompt (sim_sound run hooks); kept across RUN/BOOT and
controller clears.  Power on restores the spindle loops silenced by power
off.

SET HKn ONLINE/OFFLINE at the prompt wait until the drive is up to speed
or at rest (SPINUP, SPINDOWN); SET -N returns at once.

Common spindle support for removable-media disks (sim_spindle_*, own
timers, wall time at the prompt, waiting), used by the RK611 and the
RL11: RL01/RL02 realism mode with ONLINE/LOAD and OFFLINE/UNLOAD as the
LOAD button (40 s / 30 s), realistic RL seek and transfer times, seek sounds (rl02,
default_disk).

Massbus disks (RP): RUN/STOP button for the removable-pack drives,
realistic times per drive type (rotation speed, fitted seek curve),
seek sounds per drive type (default_disk).

MSCP disks (RQ): the RA60, the only removable-pack drive of the RA
series, gets the RUN/STOP button (SET RQn ONLINE/OFFLINE, offline-no-
volume while stopped, available attention when up to speed), AVAILABLE
with spin-down spins it down in the realism mode, realistic RA60 times
and seek sounds (ra60, default_disk).  SHOW RLn SPINDLE ends its line.

RB730 (VAX-11/730): the RB02 (an RL02) gets the LOAD button and the
realism mode (stopped drive: not ready, drive and spin error, so VMS sees
the medium offline), realistic RB02 and RB80 times, seek sounds (rl02
and rm80, default_disk).

MSCP disks (RQ), RC25: the removable RC25 and the fixed RCF25 (next
unit) share one spindle and one actuator.  SET RQn ONLINE/OFFLINE on
either unit is the Run button; in the realism mode the drive does not
start without a cartridge, spin-up 60 s / spin-down 30 s (SPINUPRC25,
SPINDOWNRC25), realistic RC25 times (2850 rpm, seek 10/35/55 ms, 31 ms
per track) and seek sounds (rc25, default_disk); a realistic configuration is
required (RC25 pairs with even/odd unit numbers on a KLESI, which only
connects RC25 drives), AVAILABLE with spin-down stops the whole drive,
KLESI controller timeout 15 s and ABORT of queued commands only.  RC25
geometry 31 x 2 x 821 in both modes.  sim_sound: no fixed limit on the
number of spindles, unit loops and run hooks; SET SOUND ENABLED
configuration checks of devices.

This patch applies on top of opensimh_6_rb730 (the RB730 fixes); it
also applies after the DMV11, DMF32, VAX 8200 and DMC patches (1-4).

